 =?UTF-8?q?=D0=B5=D0=B7=20=D0=BE=D0=B1=D1=80=D0=B0=D0=B1=D0=BE=D1=82=D1=87?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=D0=B8=D0=BA=D0=B8=20(mtk-wdt)=20=D0=B4=D0=BE=20PSCI?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PSCI SYSTEM_RESET на этой плате не перезагружает: каждая перезагрузка,
даже SysRq-b, ждала сторожа 30-70 с.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/process.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/process.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/process.c
index 322b17452..4f28705eb 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/process.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/process.c
@@ -161,11 +161,18 @@ void machine_restart(char *cmd)
 	if (efi_enabled(EFI_RUNTIME_SERVICES))
 		efi_reboot(reboot_mode, NULL);
 
+	/*
+	 * BF7: restart handlers first. On this board PSCI SYSTEM_RESET never
+	 * resets: every reboot, even SysRq-b, waited 30-70 s for a watchdog
+	 * timeout (2026-09-24, timed by the USB console dropping). The
+	 * mtk-wdt restart handler (priority 128) does the usual MediaTek
+	 * software reset at once; PSCI stays as the fallback.
+	 */
+	do_kernel_restart(cmd);
+
 	/* Now call the architecture specific reboot code. */
 	if (arm_pm_restart)
 		arm_pm_restart(reboot_mode, cmd);
-	else
-		do_kernel_restart(cmd);
 
 	/*
 	 * Whoops - the architecture was unable to reboot.
-- 
